title: 'HRMP: let a migration hand its deposits to `pallet-hrmp-para`'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    A migration that moves the relay chain's HRMP channel deposits to the parachain holding them
    hands each deposit to `pallet-hrmp-para` through `ReceiveMigratedDeposits`, keyed by one side
    of one channel (`DepositKey`). The pallet holds or releases so that the side holds the migrated
    amount, or as much of it as the paying para can cover, and reports it with `DepositMigrated`.
    A side is one deposit: what it held is overridden, so a deposit delivered twice is held once.

    `ReceiveMigratedDeposits` replaces `ReceiveMigratedChannels` and `MigratedChannel` in
    `hrmp-primitives`.

crates:
- name: pallet-hrmp-para
  bump: major
- name: hrmp-primitives
  bump: major
